(Bug #93 part B. A fresh dynamic buffer's capacity is 4096, not 0 - the
 runtime's INITIAL_BUF_CAP. size starts at 0 and stays independent of
 capacity; a small append grows size but not capacity, since 4096 already
 has room.)

a buffer called b.
Print "capacity: {b's capacity}".
Print "size: {b's size}".

Append "hi" to b.
Print "capacity after append: {b's capacity}".
Print "size after append: {b's size}".
